Package: pam-device-auth
Version: 0.5.6
Architecture: amd64
Depends: libc6, openssh-server (>= 1:9.6p1)
Recommends: sssd-ldap, libnss-sss, libpam-sss, sssd-dbus
Maintainer: Norbert Krucky <nk@dev.nk-it.cloud>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/NK-IT-CLOUD/pam-device-auth
Description: Two-factor SSH login: directory key + OIDC device grant (RFC 8628)
 Identity, groups, home directory and the sudo password come from an LDAP
 directory via SSSD/NSS; pam-device-auth adds the OIDC Device Authorization
 Grant (Keycloak, Auth0, Okta, Authentik) as a second factor for every SSH
 login. Works headless and on OpenSSH 10.2+. Statically linked Go helper,
 zero external dependencies.
